            <!-- SECTION 3: BEST PRACTICES & POLICY GUIDELINES -->
            <section class="guide-section">
                <div class="guide-container">
                    <div class="guide-split-card">
                        <div class="guide-split-content">
                            <h3>Key Leave Policies Every HR Department Must Establish</h3>
                            <p>Having clear, transparent rules prevents ambiguity, eliminates favoritism, and ensures consistent workforce operations throughout the year.</p>
                            <ul class="guide-checklist">
                                <li>
                                    <i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill"></i>
                                    <span><strong>Advance Notice Periods:</strong> Require 7–14 days prior notice for planned vacations; same-day notification for medical emergencies.</span>
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill"></i>
                                    <span><strong>Sandwich Leave Rule:</strong> Clearly define whether weekends and holidays falling between leave days count towards leave balance.</span>
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill"></i>
                                    <span><strong>Carry-Forward Caps:</strong> Set explicit limits on maximum unused earned leaves rolling into the new financial year (e.g., max 30 days).</span>
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill"></i>
                                    <span><strong>Blackout Windows:</strong> Designate critical project release or audit periods where non-emergency leaves require special leadership sign-off.</span>
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="guide-split-highlight blue-box">
                            <h4><i class="bi bi-info-circle-fill"></i> Pro Tip: The Sandwich Leave Rule</h4>
                            <p>
                                If Friday and Monday are applied as leave, does Saturday and Sunday count as 4 days of leave or 2? 
                                A transparent HR policy documented in your company's guidelines removes confusion and builds trust with your workforce.
                            </p>
                            <hr style="margin: 18px 0; border-color: rgba(30, 64, 175, 0.15);" />
                            <h4><i class="bi bi-lightbulb-fill"></i> Annual Leave Encashment</h4>
                            <p>
                                Unused Privilege Leaves can be encashed during year-end or employee exit settlements based on basic monthly salary divided by standard working days.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- SECTION 4: FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS -->
            <section class="guide-section alt-bg">
                <div class="guide-container">
                    <div class="guide-section-header">
                        <span class="guide-tag blue">Got Questions?</span>
